5.1 Verify Presistent Storage:-
=============================

"""

""
📝 PersistentVolumeClaim (PVC)A PVC is a request for storage by a developer or an application. When a database like PostgreSQL needs to store data, you don't point it directly to a physical hard drive. Instead, you create a PVC that describes what kind of storage you need.
""

"""

"""

""
📦 PersistentVolume (PV)A PV is the actual storage resource in the cluster. It represents a physical piece of storage—like a cloud drive (AWS EBS, Google Persistent Disk), an NFS share, or a local hard drive—that an administrator has provisioned.
""

"""

commands:-
"""	
	sudo kubectl get pvc -n datawarehouse
	sudo kubectl get pod -n datawarehouse -o wide
	sudo kubectl get pv 
"""

