STEP 5.5 — Create a PostgreSQL Backup:-
=====================================

commands:-
========

"""
	mkdir -p ~/DataWarehousing/backups
	
	sudo kubectl exec -it -n datawarehouse -- \
	pg_dump -U postgres -d DataWarehouse -Fc > ~/DataWarehousing/backups/DataWarehouse_backups.dump
	
	du -h ~/DataWarehousing/backups/DataWarehouse_backup.dump --> Result 22M
"""

STEP 5.6 — Verify the Backup:-
============================

commands:-

"""
	pg_restore -l ~/DataWareHousing/backups/DataWarehouse_backup.dump | head -30 
"""

"""
sudo kubectl cp ~/DataWareHousing/backups/DataWarehouse_backup.dump \
datawarehouse/$(sudo kubectl get pod -n datawarehouse -o jsonpath='{.items[0].metadata.name}'):/tmp/DataWarehouse_backup.dump

sudo kubectl exec -it -n datawarehouse deploy/postgres -- \
ls -lh /tmp/DataWarehouse_backup.dump

sudo kubectl exec -it -n datawarehouse deploy/postgres -- \
pg_restore -l /tmp/DataWarehouse_backup.dump | head -30

sudo kubectl exec -it -n datawarehouse deploy/postgres -- \
pg_restore -l /tmp/DataWarehouse_backup.dump | \
grep -E "fact_stock_prices|dim_company|dim_date"
"""

